<% content_for :title, "Avatar" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Avatar</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    An image with a fallback (initials) layered beneath it. No load-detection controller (rule 8):
    the fallback is always in the DOM, and the image sits on top of it, so a missing or failed image
    leaves the fallback showing on its own.
  </p>
</div>

<div id="avatar-preview">
  <%# Preview %>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
    <%# A working image, decorative -- the name sits next to it as text %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <%= render Ui::AvatarComponent.new do |avatar| %>
        <% avatar.with_image(src: "https://i.pravatar.cc/64?img=12") %>
        <% avatar.with_fallback { "JD" } %>
      <% end %>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium">Jane Doe</span>
    </div>

    <%# A failed image -- the fallback shows through on its own %>
    <%= render Ui::AvatarComponent.new(alt: "Alex Rivera") do |avatar| %>
      <% avatar.with_image(src: "https://broken.example/missing.png") %>
      <% avatar.with_fallback { "AR" } %>
    <% end %>

    <%# No image at all %>
    <%= render(Ui::AvatarComponent.new(alt: "Sam Okafor")) { |avatar| avatar.with_fallback { "SO" } } %>

    <%# Sized entirely from class: -- no size axis on the component %>
    <%= render Ui::AvatarComponent.new(alt: "Priya Nair", class: "size-12") do |avatar| %>
      <% avatar.with_image(src: "https://i.pravatar.cc/96?img=47") %>
      <% avatar.with_fallback(class: "text-base") { "PN" } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#avatar-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="avatar-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_avatar_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Slots %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Slots</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Slot</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">data-slot</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["with_image",    "avatar-image",    "The photo. Layered over the fallback; alt is always empty, since the avatar's own alt: carries the accessible name."],
        ["with_fallback", "avatar-fallback", "Initials or an icon, underneath the image. Hidden from assistive tech unless you override it."],
      ].each do |slot, data_slot, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= slot %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= data_slot %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Alt text %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Alt text</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
  <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">alt:</code> lives on
  <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">Ui::AvatarComponent</code> itself, not on the image part.
</p>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside mb-8">
  <li><strong>Omitted</strong> (the default): the avatar is decorative. Use this whenever a name is already visible as text next to it -- a comment row, a table cell with a name column. Repeating the name in alt text would just double-announce it.</li>
  <li><strong>Present</strong>: this avatar is the only identification of who it is. The root becomes <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">role="img"</code> with that <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-label</code>, and both the image and the fallback stay presentational underneath it -- one name for the whole avatar, never two.</li>
</ul>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>No Stimulus controller. The image is always in the DOM, positioned over the fallback; a missing <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">src</code> or a failed load paints nothing, so the fallback beneath it shows through on its own.</li>
  <li>No size axis: size and shape come from <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">class:</code> (the default is <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">size-8</code>).</li>
  <li>Fallback text reaches 4.5:1 on <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">--muted</code> in both light and dark mode.</li>
  <li>A caller whose fallback carries its own meaning (an icon that isn't just initials) can override the default hiding with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">avatar.with_fallback(aria: { hidden: false })</code>.</li>
</ul>
